## Interview / owner language (short)

> **Detect:** timeout ke baad success rows + same user/amount cluster.  
> **Impact:** duplicate debit / extra files.  
> **Mitigate:** write-retry band, status API, flag off auto-pay tool.  
> **Evidence:** trace + idempotency table + ledger.  
> **Root cause:** side-effect ke baad lost response + non-idempotent retry.  
> **Fix:** stable **Idempotency-Key**, unique index, GET-before-retry, HITL.  
> **KPI:** `duplicate_txn_rate → 0`, `ambiguous_failures` reconciled < SLA.

**Ek line:** Agent ko **Failed** tab bolo jab backend ne **explicit reject** diya ho; **timeout = unknown**. Unknown par **naya transaction nahi**, **purani intent ki status**.



Haan — **webhooks**, **polling**, aur kuch aur patterns **isi ambiguous-failure** scene ke liye banaye gaye hain. Magar yaad rakho: ye **duplicate rokne ka magic** nahi hain. Asli lock phir bhi **Idempotency-Key + status store** hai. Webhook/poll sirf **truth late** hain, “dobara hit mat maaro” alag rule hai.

```
User / Agent
 └── Goal: timeout ke baad guess nahi — source-of-truth pucho
      └── Context: MCP tool, payment/file, network drop
           ├── Facts: backend commit ho chuka ho sakta hai
           ├── Surfaces: HTTP response, webhook, poll API, queue, WS
           └── Risk: webhook bhi duplicate aata hai; poll storm; missed event
                └── Path A: Status API + Webhook + Idempotent handler (cloud inbuilt)
                     └── Path B: existing PG / order bus
                          └── Path C: HITL agar status unknown + money
                               └── Path D: short poll + long webhook
                                    └── Signal: PENDING / SUCCEEDED / FAILED
                                         └── Decision: SUCCEEDED → reuse; PENDING → wait; FAILED → naya attempt nahi jab tak reason explicit ho
```

---

## Pehle definition

- **Polling:** Agent/client baar-baar `GET /status?intent_id=...` karta hai. “Ab kya hua?”
- **Webhook:** Backend kaam khatam hone par **tumhare URL** par `POST` bhejta hai. “Ho gaya, ye result hai.”
- **Long-poll / SSE / WebSocket:** Connection khuli rehti hai, status **push** hota hai. Poll jitna spam nahi, webhook jitna fire-and-forget nahi.
- **Outbox + message bus:** DB commit ke saath event table, phir **Pub/Sub / EventBridge / Event Grid / Eventarc** — reliable notify.
- **Callback / redirect:** Browser/PG flow (`success_url`) — agent-only world mein kam reliable.

---

## Hierarchy — confirmation styles

```
Write start (intent_id + idempotency_key)
 └── Immediate ACK: ACCEPTED / PENDING   ← timeout yahan bhi ho sakta
      ├── Sync response (lucky path)
      ├── Polling          GET status
      ├── Webhook          POST your endpoint
      ├── Push channel     SSE / WebSocket / MQTT
      └── Reconciliation   cron / ledger compare   ← last safety net
           └── Terminal state: SUCCEEDED | FAILED | CANCELED
```

---

## Kab kaunsa

| Pattern | Kab lo | Strong | Weak |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Status poll** | Agent timeout ke **turant baad** | Simple, firewall-friendly, MCP ke saath easy | Extra calls, delayed UX |
| **Webhook** | Payment, KYC, file virus-scan, bank | Fast notify, server-push | Miss, retry storm, auth, order of events |
| **SSE / WebSocket** | Live UI, agent session open hai | Low lag | Connection toot-ti hai; mobile/serverless hard |
| **Queue / Eventarc** | Internal microservices | Retry + DLQ | User/agent tak extra hop |
| **Reconciliation job** | Money / inventory | Webhook miss bhi pakadta | Minutes late |

**Production combo (best):**  
`Write → 202 PENDING` + **short poll (agent)** + **webhook (system)** + **nightly/5-min reconcile**.

Stripe/Razorpay/GCP payments bhi yahi karte hain: API response + webhook + dashboard status. Sirf ek par mat baitho.

